.Dd September 19, 2026
.Dt BUSYBOX-RUNIT 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm busybox-runit ,
.Nm chpst ,
.Nm envdir ,
.Nm envuidgid ,
.Nm runsv ,
.Nm runsvdir ,
.Nm setuidgid ,
.Nm softlimit ,
.Nm sv ,
.Nm svc ,
.Nm svlogd ,
.Nm svok
.Nd BusyBox runit supervision tools
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm chpst
.Op Fl vP012
.Op Fl u Ar USER Ns Op : Ns Ar GRP
.Op Fl U Ar USER Ns Op : Ns Ar GRP
.Op Fl e Ar DIR
.Op Fl / Ar DIR
.Op Fl n Ar NICE
.Op Fl m Ar BYTES
.Op Fl d Ar BYTES
.Op Fl o Ar N
.Op Fl p Ar N
.Op Fl f Ar BYTES
.Op Fl c Ar BYTES
.Ar PROG ARGS
.Nm envdir
.Ar DIR PROG ARGS
.Nm envuidgid
.Ar USER PROG ARGS
.Nm runsv
.Ar DIR
.Nm runsvdir
.Op Fl P
.Op Fl s Ar SCRIPT
.Ar DIR
.Nm setuidgid
.Ar USER PROG ARGS
.Nm softlimit
.Op Fl a Ar BYTES
.Op Fl m Ar BYTES
.Op Fl d Ar BYTES
.Op Fl s Ar BYTES
.Op Fl l Ar BYTES
.Op Fl f Ar BYTES
.Op Fl c Ar BYTES
.Op Fl r Ar BYTES
.Op Fl o Ar N
.Op Fl p Ar N
.Op Fl t Ar N
.Ar PROG ARGS
.Nm sv
.Op Fl v
.Op Fl w Ar SEC
.Ar CMD SERVICE_DIR ...
.Nm svc
.Op Fl udopchaitkx
.Ar SERVICE_DIR ...
.Nm svlogd
.Op Fl tttv
.Op Fl r Ar C
.Op Fl R Ar CHARS
.Op Fl l Ar MATCHLEN
.Op Fl b Ar BUFLEN
.Ar DIR ...
.Nm svok
.Ar SERVICE_DIR
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These are the runit applets of BusyBox 1.36.1 as built for Rach2.
Nothing on the Rach2 images uses them, and the supervisors do not work
here: Rach2 registers neither
.Fn flock
nor
.Fn fchdir ,
so
.Nm runsv
fails at its lock,
.Nm runsvdir
fails after scanning its directory, and
.Nm svlogd
cannot enter its log directory; and
.Nm envdir
and
.Nm chpst Fl e
end before running their program, since reading the directory changes
into it.
.Bl -tag -width setuidgid
.It Nm chpst
Change process state, then run
.Ar PROG .
.It Nm envdir
Set environment variables from files in
.Ar DIR ,
then run
.Ar PROG .
.It Nm envuidgid
Set
.Ev UID
and
.Ev GID
to the user and group IDs of
.Ar USER ,
then run
.Ar PROG .
.It Nm runsv
Start and monitor a service and, optionally, its log service.
.It Nm runsvdir
Start a
.Nm runsv
process for each subdirectory of
.Ar DIR .
Restart each process when it exits.
.It Nm setuidgid
Set the user and group IDs to those of
.Ar USER ,
drop supplementary group IDs, and run
.Ar PROG .
.It Nm softlimit
Set soft resource limits, then run
.Ar PROG .
.It Nm sv , svc
Control services monitored by
.Nm runsv .
.It Nm svlogd
Read log data from standard input and write rotated log files in
.Ar DIR .
.It Nm svok
Check whether the
.Nm runsv
supervisor is running.
.El
.Ss sv commands
Only the first character of a command is required.
.Bl -tag -width interrupt
.It Cm status
Query service status.
.It Cm up
Start the service if it is not running; restart it if it stops.
.It Cm once
Start the service as for
.Cm up ,
but do not restart it if it stops.
.It Cm down
Send TERM and CONT to the service.
If
.Pa ./run
exits, start
.Pa ./finish
if it exists.
After it stops, do not restart the service.
.It Cm exit
Send TERM and CONT to the service and log service.
When both exit,
.Nm runsv
exits too.
.It Cm pause , cont , hup , alarm , interrupt , quit , 1 , 2 , term , kill
Send STOP, CONT, HUP, ALRM, INT, QUIT, USR1, USR2, TERM, or KILL,
respectively, to the service.
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Ss chpst
.Bl -tag -width "-U USER[:GRP]"
.It Fl u Ar USER Ns Op : Ns Ar GRP
Set the user and group IDs.
.It Fl U Ar USER Ns Op : Ns Ar GRP
Set
.Ev UID
and
.Ev GID
in the environment.
.It Fl e Ar DIR
Set environment variables from files in
.Ar DIR :
each file name not beginning with a period becomes a variable, its value
the file's first 255 bytes with trailing whitespace removed, and an empty
file unsets the variable.
On Rach2 the option ends the program before it runs, as above.
.It Fl / Ar DIR
Change the root directory and the working directory to
.Ar DIR ,
as
.Xr chroot 2
describes, before running the program, which is then found from the new
root.
.It Fl n Ar NICE
Add
.Ar NICE
to the nice value.
Rach2 has no priority calls, so the option reports an error and ends
before running the program.
.It Fl m Ar BYTES
Set memory limits: on Rach2, the address-space limit through the implied
.Fl a ;
the other three have no effect.
.It Fl d Ar BYTES
Limit the data segment; no effect on Rach2.
.It Fl o Ar N
Limit open files per process.
.It Fl p Ar N
Limit processes per user ID.
.It Fl f Ar BYTES
Limit output file sizes; no effect on Rach2.
.It Fl c Ar BYTES
Limit core file size; no effect on Rach2.
.It Fl v
Produce verbose output.
.It Fl P
Create a process group.
.It Fl 0 , 1 , 2
Close standard input, standard output, or standard error, respectively.
.El
.Ss runsvdir
.Bl -tag -width "-s SCRIPT"
.It Fl P
Put each
.Nm runsv
process in a new session.
.It Fl s Ar SCRIPT
Run
.Ar SCRIPT
with the signal number after processing a signal.
.El
.Ss softlimit
.Bl -tag -width "-a BYTES"
.It Fl a Ar BYTES
Limit the total size of all segments.
.It Fl m Ar BYTES
Equivalent to
.Fl d Ar BYTES Fl s Ar BYTES Fl l Ar BYTES Fl a Ar BYTES ;
on Rach2 only the address-space limit takes effect.
.It Fl d Ar BYTES
Limit the data segment; no effect on Rach2.
.It Fl s Ar BYTES
Limit the stack segment; no effect on Rach2.
.It Fl l Ar BYTES
Limit locked memory; no effect on Rach2.
.It Fl o Ar N
Limit open files per process.
.It Fl p Ar N
Limit processes per user ID.
.It Fl f Ar BYTES
Limit output file sizes; no effect on Rach2.
.It Fl c Ar BYTES
Limit core file size; no effect on Rach2.
.It Fl r Ar BYTES
Limit resident set size; no effect on Rach2.
.It Fl t Ar N
Limit CPU time; no effect on Rach2, which sends no SIGXCPU.
.El
.Ss svc
.Bl -tag -width "-pchaitk"
.It Fl u
Start the service if it is not running; restart it if it stops.
.It Fl d
Send TERM and CONT if the service is running; do not restart it.
.It Fl o
Start the service if it is not running; do not restart it.
.It Fl p , c , h , a , i , t , k
Send STOP, CONT, HUP, ALRM, INT, TERM, or KILL, respectively, to the service.
.It Fl x
Make
.Nm runsv
exit as soon as the service is down.
.El
.Ss svlogd
.Bl -tag -width "-R CHARS"
.It Fl r Ar C
Replace non-printable characters with
.Ar C .
.It Fl R Ar CHARS
Also replace the characters in
.Ar CHARS
with
.Ar C ,
which defaults to
.Ql _ .
.It Fl t
Timestamp with
.Ql @tai64n .
.It Fl tt
Timestamp with
.Ql yyyy-mm-dd_hh:mm:ss.sssssssss .
.It Fl ttt
Timestamp with
.Ql yyyy-mm-ddThh:mm:ss.sssssssss .
.It Fl v
Produce verbose output.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width DIR/config
.It Pa DIR/config
Modify the behavior of
.Nm svlogd .
.Ql sSIZE
sets the rotation size, default 1000000; 0 disables rotation.
.Ql nNUM
sets the number of files to retain.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm svok
exits with 0 if the supervisor is running, 100 if it is not, or 111 with
an error message if
.Ar SERVICE_DIR
does not exist.
